type: software
title: "Система оценки качества ответов больших языковых моделей по новостным текстам стран Восточной Азии"
abstract: >-
  Bachelor's thesis repository (Faculty of Computational Mathematics and Cybernetics,
  Lomonosov Moscow State University): a system for evaluating the quality of large language
  model answers to questions about East Asian news texts in a cross-lingual setting (questions
  in Russian, sources in Chinese-language media). The object of measurement is the answer
  a = f(q), where q is a frozen snapshot of the corpus, not the model that produced it. The
  system comprises a formal problem statement with a time-invariance predicate that restricts
  the golden set to static questions whose answers do not change over time; a golden set with
  reference answers, aliases and supporting document identifiers, annotated independently by
  three annotators with Krippendorff's alpha of at least 0.67; a family of reference-based,
  citation, abstention and retrieval metrics including a language-model judge that is
  meta-evaluated separately for reliability and validity (Spearman correlation with human
  ratings of at least 0.5); and a statistical protocol (paired bootstrap, Wilcoxon signed-rank
  test with Holm correction, Cliff's delta) for comparing systems by a composite score. The
  object of study is the industrial system "Chinese Media Analysis" (Institute of Oriental
  Studies, Russian Academy of Sciences) over a corpus of media from the PRC, Taiwan, Hong Kong
  and Singapore (23.9 million chunks); it is compared with six open models without retrieval
  and with a shared retriever (13 systems).
